<title>DENMARK: Danish Feb North Sea gas production falls 15.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish Feb North Sea gas production falls 15.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) production of gas from its North Sea fields fell 15.8 percent in February, to 630 million cubic metres from 748 million cubic metres in January, a spokesman for operator A.P. Moeller Group told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields which make the country the fourth-biggest offshore gas producer in western Europe after Norway, Britain and the Netherlands.</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc, own 46 percent and 15 percent, respectively.</p>
<p>    (Million cubic metres)   Feb 97    Jan 97   Feb 96</p>
<p>    Total production	     630	748	 500</p>
<p>-- Steve Weizman, Copenhagen Newsroom 45-33-969650</p>
</text>
